# docs/data/events.json is a build artifact: the daily workflow rewrites it and
# pushes, so a local commit will collide with the bot sooner or later.
#
# `-merge` marks it unmergeable, so git stops with a conflict instead of trying
# to combine two versions.  That matters: a `union` driver was tried first and
# silently interleaved both copies into a file that parsed nowhere, which then
# got committed.  There is never anything to merge here -- the file is
# regenerated from the sources:
#
#     python -m collector.build && git add docs/data/events.json
#
docs/data/events.json -merge linguist-generated=true
